#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186264499 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "045722b6-b558-522b-86e1-322c64e2848f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Limit of a Rational Function with a Radical in the Denominator"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e9522321-d07c-5a20-b5a9-f2ebff52419f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264501} {:answer/id #uuid "1b2dbd48-6baf-5e15-bbfb-b49df51606ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{7}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264502} {:answer/id #uuid "934ab8eb-0b43-5dbc-8b63-94acc00d4e00" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264503} {:answer/id #uuid "136c30fa-9044-52a8-8a49-837a101f76ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\sqrt{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264504} {:answer/id #uuid "f330557c-b754-5f71-a0c9-29586f4eec50" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264505}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1b2dbd48-6baf-5e15-bbfb-b49df51606ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{7}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264502} :answer-field/id #uuid "cdaf86b8-fe13-5914-bc47-1912531cc01e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264500}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4657fda3-adb3-52a6-b9ad-8af5d9861fcc" :question/math-academy-id "q-101288" :question/problem "${lim}_{x\\to 2}\\frac{x-2}{\\sqrt{3x+1}-\\sqrt{7}}=$" :question/worked-solution "If we attempt to evaluate the limit by simply evaluating the function at $x=2$, we get an indeterminate form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 2}\\frac{x-2}{\\sqrt{3x+1}-\\sqrt{7}} & =\\frac{2-2}{\\sqrt{3(2)+1}-\\sqrt{7}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2-2}{\\sqrt{7}-\\sqrt{7}} \\\\  & =\\frac{0}{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we need to first simplify the limit. Since the radical is in the denominator, we can multiply the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the denominator. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 2}\\frac{x-2}{\\sqrt{3x+1}-\\sqrt{7}} & ={lim}_{x\\to 2}\\frac{(x-2)(\\sqrt{3x+1}+\\sqrt{7})}{(\\sqrt{3x+1}-\\sqrt{7})(\\sqrt{3x+1}+\\sqrt{7})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 2}\\frac{(x-2)(\\sqrt{3x+1}+\\sqrt{7})}{(\\sqrt{3x+1})^{2}-(\\sqrt{7})^{2}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 2}\\frac{(x-2)(\\sqrt{3x+1}+\\sqrt{7})}{3x+1-7} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 2}\\frac{(x-2)(\\sqrt{3x+1}+\\sqrt{7})}{3x-6} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 2}\\frac{(x-2)(\\sqrt{3x+1}+\\sqrt{7})}{3(x-2)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 2}\\frac{\\sqrt{3x+1}+\\sqrt{7}}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3(2)+1}+\\sqrt{7}}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{7}+\\sqrt{7}}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{7}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186353853 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "045722b6-b558-522b-86e1-322c64e2848f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Limit of a Rational Function with a Radical in the Denominator"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "24cf0ad0-ab60-5a30-9ac4-3231c0c94e85" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353855} {:answer/id #uuid "b6726a7e-b16a-5b7e-9ea4-282df7d3b681" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353856}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "24cf0ad0-ab60-5a30-9ac4-3231c0c94e85" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353855} :answer-field/id #uuid "686cebf8-b881-5bb8-aaf1-d98b1c24baa1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353854}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c2769d9a-ddb4-50d7-a6fa-fc81c76cd49c" :question/math-academy-id "q-302322" :question/problem "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{x+1}-1}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "If we attempt to evaluate the limit by simply evaluating the function at $x=0$, we get an indeterminate form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{x+1}-1} & =\\frac{0}{\\sqrt{0+1}-1}=\\frac{0}{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we need to first simplify the limit. Since the radical is in the denominator, we can multiply the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the denominator. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{x+1}-1} & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{x(\\sqrt{x+1}+1)}{(\\sqrt{x+1}-1)(\\sqrt{x+1}+1)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{x(\\sqrt{x+1}+1)}{(\\sqrt{x+1})^{2}-{1}^{2}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{x(\\sqrt{x+1}+1)}{(x+1)-1} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{x(\\sqrt{x+1}+1)}{x} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{\\cancel{x}(\\sqrt{x+1}+1)}{\\cancel{x}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}(\\sqrt{x+1}+1) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{0+1}+1 \\\\  & =1+1 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259823 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "045722b6-b558-522b-86e1-322c64e2848f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Limit of a Rational Function with a Radical in the Denominator"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6a3764b5-0eaf-586c-8cf3-8754e6fd6227" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259825}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6a3764b5-0eaf-586c-8cf3-8754e6fd6227" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259825} :answer-field/id #uuid "6b5640e3-e135-59a8-88e8-a44d496816e2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259824}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7c248ff4-4847-5ae9-892d-0c9714b8f260" :question/math-academy-id "q-338517" :question/problem "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{{x}^{2}-9}{\\sqrt{x+1}-2}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "If we attempt to evaluate the limit by simply evaluating the function at $x=0$, we get an indeterminate form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{{x}^{2}-9}{\\sqrt{x+1}-2} & =\\frac{{3}^{2}-9}{\\sqrt{3+1}-2}=\\frac{0}{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we need to first simplify the limit. Since the radical is in the denominator, we can multiply the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the denominator. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{{x}^{2}-9}{\\sqrt{x+1}-2} & ={lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{({x}^{2}-9)(\\sqrt{x+1}+2)}{(\\sqrt{x+1}-2)(\\sqrt{x+1}+2)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{(x-3)(x+3)(\\sqrt{x+1}+2)}{(\\sqrt{x+1})^{2}-{2}^{2}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{(x-3)(x+3)(\\sqrt{x+1}+2)}{(x+1)-4} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{(x-3)(x+3)(\\sqrt{x+1}+2)}{x-3} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{\\cancel{(x-3)}(x+3)(\\sqrt{x+1}+2)}{\\cancel{x-3}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 3}\\,(x+3)(\\sqrt{x+1}+2) \\\\  & =(3+3)(\\sqrt{3+1}+2) \\\\  & =6(4) \\\\  & =24.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078844 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a441c8ef-b5b3-5438-97b9-53e4eb7b2d75" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Limit of a Rational Function with a Radical in the Numerator"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b723c2d8-136e-55e3-9269-c9ffc1c383dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\infty" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186076276} {:answer/id #uuid "bc87ffc9-a21b-54af-9bb2-7c7d249fc266" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186076277} {:answer/id #uuid "c4c856d2-7537-5bef-a185-5c8f6b2fb629" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186076278} {:answer/id #uuid "564a7da1-875b-5dcb-ad94-b9442d893838" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "DNE" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186076279} {:answer/id #uuid "773152cc-8be4-535b-9cf6-f78f4694116c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186076280}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "773152cc-8be4-535b-9cf6-f78f4694116c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186076280} :answer-field/id #uuid "98f724b2-e264-5a10-9f7c-c929906f27ac" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186076275}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3147ba88-441f-5986-9848-1ff065e91dc8" :question/math-academy-id "q-4466" :question/problem "Evaluate ${lim}_{x\\to 4}\\frac{\\sqrt{x}-2}{x-4}.$" :question/worked-solution "If we attempt to evaluate the limit, we get an indeterminate form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 4}\\frac{\\sqrt{x}-2}{x-4} & =\\frac{\\sqrt{4}-2}{4-4}=\\frac{0}{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we need to first simplify the limit. Since the radical is in the numerator, we can multiply the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the numerator. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 4}\\frac{\\sqrt{x}-2}{x-4} & ={lim}_{x\\to 4}\\frac{(\\sqrt{x}-2)(\\sqrt{x}+2)}{(x-4)(\\sqrt{x}+2)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 4}\\frac{{(\\sqrt{x})}^{2}-{2}^{2}}{(x-4)(\\sqrt{x}+2)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 4}\\frac{x-4}{(x-4)(\\sqrt{x}+2)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 4}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}+2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4}+2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186264545 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a441c8ef-b5b3-5438-97b9-53e4eb7b2d75" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Limit of a Rational Function with a Radical in the Numerator"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4c6042be-68e6-5614-b52d-6187961da820" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264547} {:answer/id #uuid "c39a0edb-c621-53b4-845d-43c733153aa0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264548} {:answer/id #uuid "d5a9454a-fd37-5f0a-94d4-516aff72fd65" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264549} {:answer/id #uuid "659ab017-b94c-5292-b78f-13b403f41670" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{DNE}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264550} {:answer/id #uuid "23eb41e1-df86-5d23-b317-2c9449eb29ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264551}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d5a9454a-fd37-5f0a-94d4-516aff72fd65" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264549} :answer-field/id #uuid "c3bffd14-44d5-5a70-ab62-289469c303c9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264546}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c2192068-6d96-59a7-8da5-820238c32032" :question/math-academy-id "q-46838" :question/problem "Evaluate ${lim}_{x\\to {25}^{-}}\\frac{2x-10\\sqrt{x}}{x-25}.$" :question/worked-solution "If we attempt to evaluate the limit, we get an indeterminate form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {25}^{-}}\\frac{2x-10\\sqrt{x}}{x-25} & =\\frac{50-10\\sqrt{25}}{25-25}=\\frac{0}{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we need to first simplify the limit. Since the radical is in the numerator, we can multiply the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the numerator. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {25}^{-}}\\frac{2x-10\\sqrt{x}}{x-25} & ={lim}_{x\\to {25}^{-}}\\frac{2(x-5\\sqrt{x})}{x-25} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to {25}^{-}}\\frac{2(x-5\\sqrt{x})(x+5\\sqrt{x})}{(x-25)(x+5\\sqrt{x})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to {25}^{-}}\\frac{2({x}^{2}-{(5\\sqrt{x})}^{2})}{(x-25)(x+5\\sqrt{x})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to {25}^{-}}\\frac{2({x}^{2}-25x)}{(x-25)(x+5\\sqrt{x})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to {25}^{-}}\\frac{2x(x-25)}{(x-25)(x+5\\sqrt{x})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to {25}^{-}}\\frac{2x}{x+5\\sqrt{x}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(25)}{25+5\\sqrt{25}} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
